+# Tasks
+
+## 1. Persistence and transaction support
+
+- [x] 1.1 Add `withTransaction(db, fn)` to `src/db.ts` (BEGIN/COMMIT/ROLLBACK) and verify `npm run build` passes.
+- [x] 1.2 Add `OrderRepository.applyCoupon(id, couponCode, discountCents, finalAmountCents)` to update the order's coupon columns; verify by reading the order back in a test.
+- [x] 1.3 Add `CouponRepository.recordRedemption(orderId, code, discountCents, createdAt)` that inserts into `coupon_redemptions` and increments `coupons.used_count`; verify with a repository-level assertion.
+
+## 2. Order service: apply coupon
+
+- [x] 2.1 Inject `CouponRepository` and `Db` into `OrderService` and update `src/app.ts` wiring; verify `npm run build`.
+- [x] 2.2 Implement `OrderService.applyCoupon(id, couponCode)` ordering the checks: order exists/pending/no coupon, coupon exists/active/valid window, minimum amount, usage limit. Verify each error code with tests.
+- [x] 2.3 Implement the discount calculation (FIXED value, PERCENT floored, `maxDiscountCents` cap, clamp to order amount) and persist order + redemption + usage inside `withTransaction`; verify fixed, percent, floored, capped and over-amount cases return expected `discountCents`/`finalAmountCents`.
+
+## 3. HTTP route
+
+- [x] 3.1 Register `POST /orders/:id/apply-coupon` in `src/routes/orders.ts` using `parseId`; verify a 200 response includes the coupon code and computed amounts, and a missing `couponCode` returns 400 `INVALID_REQUEST`.
+
+## 4. Integration verification
+
+- [x] 4.1 Add integration tests covering the happy path plus unknown order/coupon, non-pending order, disabled/expired/not-yet-valid coupon, minimum amount and usage limit; run `npm test` and ensure all pass.
+- [x] 4.2 Run `npm run build` and confirm the full existing suite still passes.
+
+## Workflow follow-up
+
+- Archive the change with `openspec archive apply-coupon-to-order` after review.
+- Sync the `order-coupons` capability into `openspec/specs/` on archive.
